# The source extracts go here, and EVERY *.csv in this directory is read as one
# (SPEC 3.1). Nothing is ignored: the results are written one level up, so
# there is no output down here to exclude and no naming rule to observe.
#
# This file exists to keep the directory in git, which does not track empty
# ones - without it the merge on a fresh clone fails with
# "no source CSVs in merge/input/" before it can say anything more useful.
#
# Whether the extracts themselves are committed is SPEC 12.8 and still open.
# They are the evidence behind every project file, but may carry contact data,
# and merge_manifest.json records each one's sha256 either way.

01-sap-export.csv
02-cmdb-dump.csv
03-team-umfrage.csv

